<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer gets two textile machine orders.</title>
<headline>Sulzer gets two textile machine orders.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer Rueti, a unit of Swiss-based Sulzer AG, said it had received two orders for a total of 280 textile machines.</p>
<p>The value of the order was not given.</p>
<p>The orders came from a U.S. textile manufacturer and from a Mexican textile factory, Sulzer said.  </p>
<p>The orders were for air jet weaving machines.</p>
<p>The Mexican order, for plants in Mexico City and Veracruz, totalled 180 machines.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Sulzer, in response to an enquiry, later said the orders were worth around 20 million Swiss francs in total.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
